Tell a placed call whose offer write failed from one that failed before writing anything.

Origin: fazer-ai/whatsapp-connector, upstream meowcaller code (not from a pull request).

Why: the connector keeps a `call.start` attempt standing when its failure may have rung the callee's phone, so a redelivery under the same idempotency key does not ring it again, and releases it otherwise, so a retry after a transient failure can still place the call. Call fails in several places before the offer goes out (no own LID, device discovery, a peer with no devices, callKey encryption, the device identity) and in one after it: the offer write. Only that one can have rung the phone, and the error text is the only thing that told them apart.

The offer write's failure now wraps ErrSendOffer, exported, beside the error SendNode returned. The message is unchanged ("send offer: ..."), and no other path changes.

diff --git a/engine.go b/engine.go
index 0c575f9..d75111a 100644
--- a/engine.go
+++ b/engine.go
@@ -602,13 +602,18 @@ func (e *engine) placeCall(ctx context.Context, target string, opts CallOptions)
 		// The caller gets no Call to hang up, so the registration and its key
 		// material would otherwise stay in e.calls for the client's lifetime.
 		e.finishCall(callID, "offer_failed")
-		return nil, fmt.Errorf("send offer: %w", err)
+		return nil, fmt.Errorf("%w: %w", ErrSendOffer, err)
 	}
 	e.c.log.Info().Str("call_id", callID).Bool("video", opts.Video).Msg("offer sent; media starts when the relay endpoint arrives")
 	e.c.diag.Emit("meta", map[string]any{"event": "offer_sent", "call_id": callID, "peer_lid": peerLID.String(), "direction": "out", "video": opts.Video})
 	return call, nil
 }
 
+// ErrSendOffer is a placed call whose offer write failed: the offer may have reached
+// WhatsApp, and the callee's phone may be ringing. Every other error Call returns comes
+// before that write.
+var ErrSendOffer = errors.New("send offer")
+
